title: c2c doctor overclaims LIVE app-server delivery in the degraded no-thread-loaded case
updated_at: "2026-07-11T16:58:06Z"
---
c2c doctor/health classifies an 'online-attached' app-server codex session as LIVE managed delivery even when the deliver loop is DEGRADED because no frontend thread ever loaded (C2c_codex_deliver_loop outcome.degraded=true, thread_id=None). The degraded flag is runtime-only and not persisted where the doctor (which reads persisted state) can see it. Fix: persist the degraded/thread-loaded signal (e.g. into the instance/registration state the doctor reads) and surface 'app-server (degraded: no thread loaded)' with remediation instead of a bare LIVE. Found in B131 opus review (deferred out-of-scope there).